## 📦 What's Included (Phase 1)

### ✅ Extension Code
- `src/extension.ts` — Entry point, lifecycle, commands, status bar
- `src/manager.ts` — Binary detection, spawning, management
- `src/server.ts` — MCP server adapter over stdio
- `src/http-client.ts` — HTTP wrapper for poml API

### ✅ Build & Deployment
- `scripts/build-binaries.sh` — Cross-compile Go for 6 platforms
- `.github/workflows/build-release.yml` — Automated CI/CD (tag → build → publish)
- `package.json` — Extension manifest with all scripts and metadata
- `jest.config.js` — Testing framework
- `.eslintrc.js` — Code linting

### ✅ Configuration
- `tsconfig.json` — TypeScript strict mode
- `.prettierrc` — Code formatting
- `.vscode/launch.json` — Debug configuration
- `.vscode/tasks.json` — Build tasks

### ✅ Binary Distribution
- `vscode-extension/bin/{darwin,linux,windows}/{amd64,arm64}/poml[.exe]`
- All 6 platform binaries (built by script, bundled in extension)
- Size: ~100 MB total, ~15 MB per platform

### ✅ Documentation
- `VSCODE_EXTENSION_SUMMARY.md` — Overview & implementation details
- `ARCHITECTURE_SUMMARY.md` — Visual diagrams & architecture
- `DEVELOPER_REFERENCE.md` — Complete reference guide
- `RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md` — Pre-release & publishing guide
- `NEXT_STEPS.md` — Actionable next steps (weeks 1–4)
- POML docs in `docs/` directory

### ✅ Test Templates
- `src/integration.test.ts` — E2E test template
- `src/http-client.test.ts` — HTTP client test skeleton

